        "original_id": "6f9aee95-1ffb-5278-9a5a-f42dd0ae3ec3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Beatrice Willard, Richard Nixon, Gerald Ford\n- Organizations: Council on Environmental Quality, U.S. presidency, Vice Presidency, U.S. Congress\n- Roles: Adviser, President of the United States, Vice President of the United States, U.S. Representative, U.S. Senator\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Nixon served as the 36th Vice President of the United States from 1953 to 1961.\n- Richard Nixon served as a U.S. Representative and a U.S. Senator from California before becoming vice president.\n- Richard Nixon was the 37th President of the United States from 1969 to 1974.\n- Richard Nixon resigned from office in 1974, making him the only U.S. president to resign.\n- In her later years, Beatrice Willard advised U.S. presidents Richard Nixon and Gerald Ford.\n- Beatrice Willard was the first woman on the Council on Environmental Quality.",
